add('K64R2ScoutQuotesS198', 'scout', `Independently re-open S198 and verify every cell of its registry row and every located quote.
Row: grep '^| S198 ' ${LANE}/corpus/SOURCES.md. Fetch https://docs.jj-vcs.dev/v0.46.0/technical/concurrency/ and https://docs.jj-vcs.dev/latest/technical/concurrency/ with curl -sSL (UA 'Mozilla/5.0 (kumitate-r64)'); sha256sum each against the capture ${CAP}/jj-v0.46.0-technical-concurrency.html and the pin in ${LANE}/.ufo/pins/source-captures.json (S198). ${NORM}. For each '- S198 —' bullet of ${ENTRY} '## Located quotes' (and the Gate quote in ${LANE}/corpus/lessons/round-64.md): prove it occurs in the capture AND the live page (count occurrences), word count <= 25, name its heading. Check the anchor claims in the row ('§ Operation log, its first three paragraphs'), the claim 'normalised text equals the v0.45.1 rendering (8572 chars both)' (fetch https://docs.jj-vcs.dev/v0.45.1/technical/concurrency/ and compute), and 'the operation log is the most important piece of the lock-free design' vs the page's own wording. Report mismatches with exact replacement text.`, ['coverage'], 're-open S198');

add('K64R2ScoutQuotesS199', 'scout', `Independently re-open S199 and verify every cell of its registry row and every located quote.
Row: grep '^| S199 ' ${LANE}/corpus/SOURCES.md. Fetch https://firefox-source-docs.mozilla.org/contributing/jujutsu.html with curl -sSL (UA 'Mozilla/5.0 (kumitate-r64)'); sha256sum against ${CAP}/firefox-jujutsu.html and the pin for S199. ${NORM}. For each '- S199 —' bullet of ${ENTRY} and the Gate quote in ${LANE}/corpus/lessons/round-64.md: prove it occurs in capture and live page, <= 25 words, name its heading. Check the row's claim that Firefox's 'mach vcs-setup sets snapshot.auto-update-stale=true' (quote the page), that the page is the last content heading before § Git Tricks, the body sha256/size in the anchor cell, and the tier argument (A for a deployment's own contributor doc?). Also check whether the page has changed since the capture (Last-Modified header, a second fetch). Report mismatches with exact replacement text.`, ['coverage'], 're-open S199');

add('K64R2ScoutQuotesS200', 'scout', `Independently re-open S200 (and its relation to held row S067) and verify every cell of its row and every located quote.
Row: grep '^| S200 ' and '^| S067 ' ${LANE}/corpus/SOURCES.md. Fetch https://docs.jj-vcs.dev/v0.46.0/working-copy/, https://docs.jj-vcs.dev/latest/working-copy/ and https://docs.jj-vcs.dev/v0.45.1/working-copy/ and the raw S067 URL; sha256sum the first against ${CAP}/jj-v0.46.0-working-copy.html and the pin for S200. ${NORM}. For each '- S200 —' bullet of ${ENTRY} and the Gate quote: occurs in the S200 capture and live page; which of them ALSO occur in the v0.45.1 rendering (so S067 grounds them) and which only in v0.46.0 (the 'remove' sentences). Judge: is S200 a second row about one document (CORPUS rule 4) or a justified version row? Is the scope cell ('the lane's S067 holds the same pages at the host's v0.45.1') true? Verify with the host binary that 'jj workspace remove' is absent (jj workspace --help) and that the entry never relies on it for an outcome key. Report mismatches with exact replacement text.`, ['coverage', 'adjacency'], 're-open S200 vs S067');

add('K64R2ScoutRejects', 'scout', `Independently re-judge the assimilation gate decisions of the round (the lane's own gate; a non-author closure will spot-check later, make that check cheap and exact).
Read the '## Gate' section of ${LANE}/corpus/lessons/round-64.md. For the ADMIT (merged entry) and for each REJECT of the staged jj entries and amendments (${ROUTE.staged}/knowledge/corpus/knowledge/jj-*.md and agent-isolation-substrates-amendment-*.md) re-open the staged file and the cited campaign transcript paths named there and check each stated reason is TRUE (e.g. 'cites a campaign transcript path the lane cannot cite' — does the staged file's source line really cite only that path; 'superseded by the merged entry' — does the merged entry really carry the substance; 'S295's cell pairs the S198 URL with the round-12 transcript'). Also confirm the collision numbers (136/155/S195-S197), the quarantine-slice (9 lines) and the carried rejects (re-read round-63's flip conditions). Output: per decision AGREE / DISAGREE with the exact quote from the staged file that proves it. A DISAGREE on any reject means the lesson must change; be precise.`, ['calibration', 'coverage'], 're-judge gate decisions');

add('K64R2ConnCrossClaim', 'connector', `Cross-claim pattern finder: where do C1 (report-receipt-diff) and C2 (jj seat demo) share a failure mode, and what does that say for round 65?
Read ${ROUTE.plan}, ${CTL}/CHANGES-AFTER-FREEZE.md, the wave-1 reports ${LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-64/w1/*.md (skim the VERDICT line of each, read in full: K64CriticC1Predicate, K64CriticC2Predicate, K64ReviewProbeC1, K64ReviewProbeC2, K64SentinelDemoHost, K64MutateProbes). Identify classes that recur across the two claims (a counter that can be satisfied by the claim's own author-written bytes; a gate that trusts a file the lane writes; fixture-vs-real divergence; a floor that could not be met; hermeticity of a tool run on the operator host; version skew) and map each to (a) what this round did, (b) what remains, (c) the earlier round that met the same class (rounds 61–63 lessons). Propose the three most valuable round-65 claims with falsifiable before->after counters a do-nothing control cannot reach, ranked, each with the cheapest control. Also list the open L0-question candidates (operator decisions needed: counter hardening after freeze, retiring R61 probes, the epoch of Q60). Deliver ${OUT('K64R2ConnCrossClaim')}/round65-candidates.md.`, ['calibration', 'adjacency'], 'cross-claim classes and r65 candidates');

add('K64R2ConnTrace', 'connector', `Traceability matrix for the C2 entry: connect every sentence of ${ENTRY} to its support, across the lane's own corpus and the world.
For each substantive sentence (>= 40): the supporting source — demo key (${DEMO}), located quote (S198/S199/S200), a sibling lane's fact (souji ${FLEET}/souji-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/jj-colocation-receipts.md; grep other lanes for jj workspace facts), a lane fact (corpus/knowledge/agent-isolation-substrates.md M1/M3/M4/M7 — verify the cited mechanism numbers say what the entry says they say), or NONE. Then list: sentences with NONE (must be [INFERENCE]-labelled or cut), contradictions with the lane's other entries (e.g. agent-isolation-substrates.md M1 says every jj command snapshots; souji's colocation note on ref import — does the new entry contradict either?), cross-lane facts the entry restates instead of citing (adjacency: report, do not absorb), and PROVINCE frontier sentences made false or stale by this entry (read ${LANE}/PROVINCE.md and ${LANE}/corpus/README.md ## Frontier). Write ${OUT('K64R2ConnTrace')}/trace.tsv and a summary of required fixes.`, ['adjacency', 'depth'], 'entry traceability');

