add('K64R2ExecCleanRoom', 'executor', `Build a clean-room second implementation of the report-receipt contract and run it differentially against ${TOOL}.
Read ONLY the contract header comment of ${TOOL} (lines 1-35) and the QUALITY.md Q61 row (${LANE}/corpus/QUALITY.md) — do not read the tool's code. In ${OUT('K64R2ExecCleanRoom')}/clean.py (python3, stdlib only) implement the finding ids and their semantics from the contract (PLACEHOLDER, TALLY_UNRECEIPTED, TALLY_CHECKS_MISMATCH, RECEIPT_MISSING, RECEIPT_EMPTY, HASH_DEAD, HASH_ORPHAN, SECTION_MISSING, SHONEN_COUNT), reading receipts at a rev with git show/ls-tree. Run both implementations over: the 37 controls (${CTL}), the 24 real reports in ${OUT('K64ExecReceiptRealRun')}/r40.md..r63.md (--round N --rev ${INT} --fleet ${FLEET}), and 30 generated mutations of the honest control. Report every disagreement (finding id sets differ), classify each as a spec ambiguity (the contract text underdetermines it: quote the sentence), a bug in the tool, or a bug in yours, and propose contract-text fixes for the ambiguities. Agreement counts: n cases, k agree.`, ['operability', 'calibration'], 'differential clean-room tool');

add('K64R2ExecRerunC1', 'executor', `Independent re-run of the C1 counter at the integrated revision, plus determinism and the P5 report arm.
In ${LANE} (read-only): git rev-parse master; run node ${ROUTE.c1probe} ${LANE} ${INT} five times (expect RECEIPT64_UNMET held=4/5 with P5 MISS report-not-given, since no report exists yet) and once with --report <a 6-heading draft you write in ${OUT('K64R2ExecRerunC1')}/report-draft.md that satisfies the six headings, four SHONEN boxes, no placeholders>: record all verdict lines and exit codes; run node ${LANE}/scripts/counter-rerun.mjs on it (read its header; contract AGREE/DISAGREE) for 5 runs. Then take the committed freeze commit ${FREEZE} and the wave-1 landing ${W1}: run the counter at each and explain every difference (P2 at ${FREEZE}: ids=6; at ${W1}: ?). Check node scripts/counter-pins.mjs reads CLEAN (the counters are pinned, unchanged since the freeze). Report a table revision -> verdict line. Also report wall time per run and any host dependency (network, HOME).`, ['operability'], 're-run C1 counter');

add('K64R2ExecRealReports', 'executor', `Re-derive the real-report numbers the lane now quotes, with the integrated tool.
${CTL}/real-reports-v2.txt lists 11 DRIFT rounds of 24 under tool v2 (13 CLEAN). Re-run: for N in 40..63 with a lane report, take the last committed blob of .ufo/reports/round-N/kumitate.md from the fleet repo (git -C ${FLEET} log --format=%h -n1 -- <path>; git -C ${FLEET} show <h>:<path>), run node ${TOOL} --lane ${LANE} --round N --report <file> --rev ${INT} --fleet ${FLEET}; compare with real-reports-v2.txt line by line; hand-classify every finding line TRUE/FALSE with the deciding command (as K64ExecReceiptRealRun did for v1: ${OUT('K64ExecReceiptRealRun')}/classification.tsv) and name each false-positive class with its report line. Then run the tool on FIRST committed blobs too (where a round has several report commits) and say whether any first-blob verdict differs from the last-blob verdict and why (the r60 case). Also run it over the other lanes' reports in ${FLEET}/.ufo/reports/round-*/ for the same round number only as a smoke test of crashes (never judge them; they are other lanes' files: read-only, no verdict claims) — report crashes, hangs (>5 s) and exit codes outside 0/1/2.`, ['operability'], 'real reports with tool v2');

add('K64R2ExecJjOtherVersion', 'executor', `Run the demo against a second jj version (version skew is the entry's declared limit; measure it).
The host has jj 0.45.1; the docs read are v0.46.0. Fetch the OFFICIAL jj v0.46.0 release binary for linux x86_64 (GitHub releases of jj-vcs/jj; verify the published checksum/signature if the release provides one; find the right asset name from the release page) into a SCRATCH directory /tmp/kumitate-r64/K64R2ExecJjOtherVersion/bin/ (do NOT install over ~/.local/bin/jj: the lane's commit helper uses the host jj) and record tool, version, channel, source URL and reason (tooling authorization: read /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md first; no pacman). Run ${DEMO} with PATH=<scratch bin>:$PATH and show the output; diff against the host-jj run key by key. Run the 21 keys 3 times. For each key that differs: what changed (wording, behaviour) and whether the entry's statements survive (the entry claims every key was measured on 0.45.1). Also run 'jj workspace remove' on 0.46.0 in a fixture and describe its effect on the seat directory and the op log (the S200 sentence 'Tracked changes are snapshotted before the directory is removed'): is it demonstrable? Deliver ${OUT('K64R2ExecJjOtherVersion')}/skew.md with a proposed amendment to the entry's version-skew paragraph.`, ['coverage', 'depth'], 'demo on jj 0.46.0');

add('K64R2ExecSupplementaryC2', 'executor', `Write the independent supplementary checker for C2 that closes what the frozen counter cannot.
The frozen counter ${ROUTE.c2probe} (J64) reads HELD at ${INT} but wave 1 showed forgeries pass it. Write ${OUT('K64R2ExecSupplementaryC2')}/supplementary-c2.mjs (node, stdlib only, reads ONLY 'git archive <rev>' bytes) with these independent arms, each printing PASS/FAIL with a reason and an overall SUPP_C2: PASS|FAIL line: (S1) archive hygiene: no symlinks in the archive tree, no '..' in the capture-pin paths; (S2) every sentence-level number in the entry's mechanism prose (grep \`[a-z_]+=[a-z0-9-]+\`) appears among the 21 Demo outcomes with the same value (catches prose that contradicts the section the counter compares); (S3) quotes re-found in the capture with a DIFFERENT normaliser than the counter's (python or independent JS: strip tags with a real parser regex, NFKC fold) and counted exactly once; (S4) the demo bytes: sha256 of scripts/jj-seat-demo.sh at the rev equals the sha256 recorded in .ufo/pins/ (add a proposed pin entry name pin.jj-seat-demo; do not write it) and the demo is run twice in a fresh TMPDIR and prints identical output; (S5) captures re-fetched live equal the pinned bytes OR differ only outside the quoted sections (report which); (S6) registry rows S198-S200 cells re-parsed by an independent column splitter. Run it at ${INT}; then run it on 4 forgeries of K64CriticC2Predicate's (${LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-64/build/K64CriticC2Predicate/evidence) and show it fails them. Deliver the script, its outputs and the forgery results.`, ['calibration', 'coverage'], 'supplementary C2 checker');

add('K64R2ExecHarmBattery', 'executor', `Harm battery: every lane gate, base versus the integrated tree.
In scratch: BASE=${BASE}; git archive ${BASE} | tar -x -C ${OUT('K64R2ExecHarmBattery')}/base and git archive ${INT} | tar -x -C ${OUT('K64R2ExecHarmBattery')}/int (never touch the lane's index). In each tree run every gate of ${LANE}/SKILL.md's '## Gate registry' that can run offline: node scripts/<gate>.mjs (no args) and --selftest for every script that has one, the sources census (/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/scripts/sources-census.sh validate --file <tree>/corpus/SOURCES.md), plan-before-ready --selftest, readme-map, proxy-check (and --strict), claims-check, kimi-census (reads the host), cite-check, cite-sources, source-capture, source-dupes, counter-pins, anchor-truth, surface-probe, omp-census, gate-mutants (if its runtime is under 5 minutes; else say skipped). Output a table gate x (base verdict+exit, int verdict+exit, changed?). A gate that moved from clean to not-clean is a HARM candidate: say why (repaired / new defect / host drift). The expected ones: proxy-check DRIFT at base AND int (A and pins to be refreshed by the L1 at close), readme-map DRIFT -> CLEAN. Anything else is a finding. Save every transcript verbatim under ${OUT('K64R2ExecHarmBattery')}/transcripts/.`, ['operability', 'calibration'], 'harm battery');

add('K64R2ExecProxyApply', 'executor', `Make the proxy repair concrete for the integrated tree.
K64ExecProxyRepair (wave 1, ${OUT('K64ExecProxyRepair')}/refresh-stanza.mjs, ${LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-64/w1/K64ExecProxyRepair.md) wrote a stanza refresher. Run it against a git archive of ${INT} (scratch) and read the diff it proposes for SCORECARD.md (the kumitate-proxy-v1 and kumitate-gate-pins-v1 blocks). Apply the diff in the scratch copy and run node scripts/proxy-check.mjs and --strict there: they must read MATCH. Then predict what the final tree will need: the L1 will still add (a) a SCORECARD '## Round 64' section and a capabilities row, (b) SKILL.md gate-registry rows, (c) LOG.md entry, (d) more files under .ufo/waves/round-64/ (A counts .mjs/.js/.sh/.py files in the tree, scripts/proxy-check.mjs:945: wave-2 build dirs add more; mutation seats copy tools there), (e) new pins for scripts/report-receipt-diff.mjs, scripts/jj-seat-demo.sh, scripts/plan-before-ready.sh (pin.<name> keys: read how K64ExecProxyRepair handled PIN_UNPINNED; does proxy-check's GATE_PINS list need the new names? the round-62 lesson: a pin key landed without teaching proxy-check = FAIL-CLOSED). Deliver a SINGLE idempotent script ${OUT('K64R2ExecProxyApply')}/close-proxy.sh that, run in the lane at close (it prints the diff and, only with --write, edits SCORECARD.md and scripts/proxy-check.mjs GATE_PINS), brings proxy-check and --strict to MATCH, with a proof on a scratch archive that adding 300 stray .mjs files then re-running it restores MATCH.`, ['operability'], 'proxy repair script');

add('K64R2ExecKimiApply', 'executor', `Make the kimi-layer honesty record concrete (routed defect D4).
K64ExecKimiDegraded (${OUT('K64ExecKimiDegraded')}/proposal.md, ${LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-64/w1/K64ExecKimiDegraded.md) proposes keeping the four missing members and marking the layer DEGRADED with the stanza restored to the governed universe. Re-verify its facts now: node ${LANE}/scripts/kimi-census.mjs and node ${LANE}/scripts/proxy-check.mjs in a scratch archive of ${INT} (kimi-census reads the host ~/.kimi-code read-only; never print member content, names only) — are the same four members still missing? Apply its patch files (kimi-census-totals-frozen.patch, scorcard-kimi-degraded.patch) in the scratch archive and run kimi-census, proxy-check and --strict: both must agree on the layer's state. Decide with evidence whether the patch is safe to integrate at close (does it change any frozen definition? does it alter the kumitate-proxy-v1 24-key contract: AXES.md and SCORECARD say v1's keys do not change meaning) and write the final minimal patch ${OUT('K64R2ExecKimiApply')}/kimi-final.patch (against ${INT}) plus the exact SCORECARD wording, or state that the honest record is a note only (no code change) and why.`, ['calibration'], 'kimi degraded record');

add('K64R2ExecWorktreeArchive', 'executor', `Worktree-versus-archive equivalence of the lane's new instruments.
The frozen counters read 'git archive <rev>' (committed bytes). Show for ${TOOL} (--selftest), ${ROUTE.demo}, ${LANE}/scripts/plan-before-ready.sh (--selftest) and the two counters: (a) the same verdict from the worktree and from a git archive of ${INT} (a stray untracked file or an uncommitted edit in the lane must not change a counter's verdict: create a stray file only in a scratch COPY of the lane, never in the lane); (b) behaviour from a read-only mount / unwritable cwd (run in a bwrap or chmod -w scratch tree; does any instrument write into the tree it judges?); (c) behaviour with HOME unset and with an unwritable TMPDIR (clean failure message and exit code, not a stack trace); (d) behaviour under 'env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/home/vgpnk/.local/bin' (what do the node and jj resolutions need). Table: instrument x scenario -> verdict/exit/stderr. Each unclean behaviour is a finding with a minimal diff in your build directory ${OUT('K64R2ExecWorktreeArchive')}/.`, ['operability'], 'worktree vs archive equivalence');

add('K64R2ExecReportSkeleton', 'executor', `Build the round-64 report skeleton that reads CLEAN under the tool, so the L1 starts from a passing document.
Read ${LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-64/plan.md, ${TOOL} header, and the previous report (git -C ${FLEET} show 8fd46e61:.ufo/reports/round-63/kumitate.md) as the house style. Write ${OUT('K64R2ExecReportSkeleton')}/report-skeleton.md with the six required sections in order (Work performed, Landed changes, Before → after measurements, Sources & frontier, Trend verdicts, SHONEN with four lines) and the lines the prompt requires (declared claims first; counting command per claim with commit; SOURCES line; Stale-lane line; tool installs; misroot sweep; SHONEN four boxes each [~] with pointer), with EVERY unknown value written as the literal text 'UNMEASURED' (not a template token: the tool flags __X__, {{X}}, XXXX, TBD, to be filled) and a list at the end of each UNMEASURED and what command fills it. Run node ${TOOL} --lane ${LANE} --round 64 --report <skeleton> --rev ${INT}: it should read CLEAN or you document each finding. Then write ${OUT('K64R2ExecReportSkeleton')}/gotchas.md: every way the TOOL will trip an honest report of this round (a hash the report cites that is not 40-hex, tallies quoted from base receipts that carry other values, cited receipt paths with trailing punctuation, tallies in prose that are plans not results, directories) with the exact phrasing that avoids each.`, ['operability'], 'report skeleton that reads clean');

add('K64R2ExecCounterRerun', 'executor', `Counter determinism and cost: run both frozen counters under ${LANE}/scripts/counter-rerun.mjs and independently.
Read the header of ${LANE}/scripts/counter-rerun.mjs (contract AGREE/DISAGREE). For ${ROUTE.c2probe} at ${INT} (J64: live fetches, jj demo): run 5 times via counter-rerun and record AGREE/DISAGREE, wall time per run, bytes fetched, whether any network flake turns J5 into MISS (simulate by running once with the network blocked: unshare -n or a bogus resolver; report the verdict line and the exit code: unreachable must be a MISS, never HELD), and whether the verdict line depends on cwd or TMPDIR. For ${ROUTE.c1probe} (R64) the same without network. Then run jj64-probe with --no-live and show it reads UNMET 7/8 with only J5 MISS (the deliberate fail-closed). Report a table and any non-determinism with its cause; each defect with a minimal diff (as text) — the counters are frozen, so this is evidence for the closure, not a patch.`, ['operability', 'calibration'], 'counter determinism');

add('K64R2ExecHashVerify', 'executor', `Verify every commit hash and artifact path the integrated corpus text cites.
Extract hex tokens (7-40 chars) that are presented as commits and every repo path in backticks from: ${LANE}/corpus/lessons/round-64.md, ${LANE}/corpus/knowledge/jj-workspace-seat-containment.md, the appended section of ${LANE}/corpus/knowledge/agent-isolation-substrates.md, the Q60/Q61/Q51-C1 rows of ${LANE}/corpus/QUALITY.md, ${LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-64/controls/CHANGES-AFTER-FREEZE.md and ${LANE}/PROVINCE.md line 21. For each: git cat-file -e <h>^{commit} in the lane and in ${FLEET}; each path: test -e relative to ${LANE} (or the fleet for .ufo/reports/ paths); each 'path:line' reference: does the line number still hold the quoted text. Output a table token/path, resolves?, note. Every dead pointer is a finding with the corrected pointer (look for the intended object: a transposed digit, a moved line, a renamed file). Do not edit files.`, ['calibration'], 'dead pointer sweep');

add('K64R2ScribeSkillFinal', 'scribe', `Produce the final SKILL.md changes as an applyable patch and prove it.
Read ${LANE}/SKILL.md's gate registry and '## Verifiable checklist' (find the last numbered item and how inline-dispatch-evidence and plan-before-ready are registered) and the wave-1 draft ${OUT('K64ScribeLogSkill')}/skill-rows.md and checklist-item.md (they describe v1 contracts; the tool is v2 now, selftest 52, 37 controls, demo v2 with 21 keys, plan-before-ready has a map arm with PBR_MAP_FROM). Write ${OUT('K64R2ScribeSkillFinal')}/skill.patch (unified diff against ${LANE}/SKILL.md at ${INT}, line anchors recomputed) adding: gate-registry rows for report-receipt-diff, jj-seat-demo, and an updated plan-before-ready row (append, never rewrite another row); checklist items with the exact commands. Apply it to a scratch copy and run node ${LANE}/scripts/claims-check.mjs and proxy-check.mjs in a scratch archive with the patched SKILL.md: report whether either reads the registry (does a row shape change the C term or any count? say which number moves by how much and how you counted). Executable without oral context: each row names command, exit codes, when to run.`, ['depth', 'operability'], 'final SKILL patch');

add('K64R2ScribeScorecardFinal', 'scribe', `Produce the final SCORECARD.md additions for the integrated state with NO unmeasured number.
Start from ${OUT('K64ScribeScorecard')}/scorecard-r64.md (written against the freeze; stale: tool v2, 52 selftest, 37 controls, demo v2 with 21 keys, controls/CHANGES-AFTER-FREEZE.md, the P2 floor ruling is resolved by the ratchet, integration commit ${INT}, the epoch of Q60). Write ${OUT('K64R2ScribeScorecardFinal')}/scorecard-final.md: the '## Round 64' section, the capabilities row for report-receipt-diff (first-working round written ONLY as the literal word UNMEASURED until the L1 confirms a HELD reading at close), the Move log row, and the round-65 planned row; every measured figure quoted with its command, every close-time value written as the literal word UNMEASURED followed by the exact command that fills it (list them at the end). Also: verify each insertion point's line number against the current ${LANE}/SCORECARD.md (it is 2971+ lines; the Capabilities table, the Move log header and the last section) and give the anchor as a unique text match, not a number. Then apply your text to a scratch copy and run node scripts/readme-map.mjs, cite-check (compare error counts before/after: it is already DRIFT at base with ~1.6k errors) and claims-check there; report any gate that changes.`, ['calibration'], 'final SCORECARD text');

add('K64R2ScribeLogFinal', 'scribe', `Write the final LOG.md entry for round 64 (append-only).
Read the last 60 lines of ${LANE}/LOG.md for the entry style, ${OUT('K64ScribeLogSkill')}/log-entry.md (wave-1 draft, stale), ${LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-64/plan.md, controls/CHANGES-AFTER-FREEZE.md, ${LANE}/corpus/lessons/round-64.md. Write ${OUT('K64R2ScribeLogFinal')}/log-entry.md: '2026-10-25 — round 64': claims, counters, frozen revision ${FREEZE}, the three lane commits so far (${FREEZE}, ${W1}, ${INT}), what wave 1 found (the P2 floor defect, twenty forgeries, the demo's non-hermetic key, the staged claim's narrowing), controls and ratchet, assimilation theme and the admit/reject, considerthese idea 2 + idea 1, mistake mined, honest limits, the open L0 questions; any value not yet measured is the literal word UNMEASURED followed by its filling command. Every number carries its command. Do not edit LOG.md.`, ['depth', 'calibration'], 'final LOG entry');

add('K64R2ScribeReportDraft', 'scribe', `Draft the round report body from evidence (the L1 edits and files it; it must read CLEAN under ${TOOL}).
Inputs: ${LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-64/{plan.md,base/,controls/CHANGES-AFTER-FREEZE.md,w1-results.json,w1/*.md}, ${LANE}/corpus/lessons/round-64.md, the previous report as house style (git -C ${FLEET} show 8fd46e61:.ufo/reports/round-63/kumitate.md), and the prompt's report contract: ${LANE}/../.ufo/prompts/kumitate-round-64.md §4 (sections in order: Work performed (names the declared claims first), Landed changes, Before → after measurements (counting command + commit per claim), Sources & frontier (census before→after, rows by tier, assimilation theme, considerthese, the sourced claim), Trend verdicts (expansion, quality, discernment), SHONEN (4 boxes: SKILL decision tables; end-to-end task logged; instructions executable; no cross-domain bleed; [~] with pointers only), plus Stale-lane line and tool installs). Write ${OUT('K64R2ScribeReportDraft')}/report-draft.md with wave 1 facts filled from results (seat counts per role from ${LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-64/w1-dispatch.json, dead seats from w1-results.json statuses and each report's existence) and everything wave-2- or close-dependent as the literal word UNMEASURED (never a template token). Include the honest limits (counter forgeries, P2 floor ratchet, wave-1 seats found frozen-defects, post-freeze control growth disclosed). Do not file it.`, ['depth', 'calibration'], 'draft report body');

add('K64R2ScribeL0Questions', 'scribe', `Draft the L0 questions this round must append to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.ufo/l0-questions.md (one line each, format '<lane> | round-<N> | <question>'; read the file's existing kumitate lines first so none duplicates an open question).
Candidates from the round: (1) post-freeze control growth under the declared ratchet when the frozen floor was unreachable (the operator may rule that a counter whose floor cannot be met must be re-frozen with a new round instead); (2) the Q60 epoch choice (round 65) versus retroactive FAIL of rounds 58/60/61/63/64; (3) the kimi layer degraded record (K_members) — retire the four members or keep DEGRADED; (4) the frozen J64/R64 counters have known holes (forgeries, porous archive boundary, privileges of the measured tree): should the next round replace them or add a bwrap-bounded runner (cap-run exists in the lane); (5) the R61 inherited probes dispatch61/doctrine61 remain unretired in prose elsewhere? (verify before asking). Keep each question decidable by yes/no or A/B with the cost of each answer stated in the same line. Write ${OUT('K64R2ScribeL0Questions')}/l0.txt (lines only) and a short note on what you verified for each (command).`, ['calibration'], 'draft L0 questions');

add('K64R2SimplifyEntry', 'simplifier', `YAGNI pass over the C2 entry ${ENTRY} that preserves every verified claim.
Find sentences that repeat another sentence, restate a table row in prose, or carry no quote/key/inference label; find limits that duplicate; find the long header lines that can be shortened without breaking J1 (source:/verified-at:/recheck: shape) or J4 (located quotes, <= 25 words). Produce ${OUT('K64R2SimplifyEntry')}/entry.simplified.md and prove with a sandbox clone (git clone --no-hardlinks of the lane into mktemp, commit the simplified file inside the clone only with -c user.name=fixture -c user.email=fixture@example.invalid; verify git -C "$C" rev-parse --show-toplevel) that node ${ROUTE.c2probe} "$C" <rev> still reads JJ64_HELD held=8/8, and that every demo key, every table row and every [INFERENCE] label survives (diff the sets). Report line counts before/after. Do not add content.`, ['depth'], 'simplify entry');

